{"id": "unknown-2026-10-17-006", "date": "2026-10-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Norway plans to use steel from decommissioned ships for construction", "content": "<p>The Norwegian state agency Enova has announced that it is allocating up to 244 million Norwegian kroner ($25.5 million) to the companies Nordic Circles and Alsaker Stål. The funding is intended for a project to reuse steel from decommissioned ships in the construction of new structures. This was reported by SteelOrbis.            . Provided the project [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://gmk.center/en/news/norway-plans-to-use-steel-from-decommissioned-ships-for-construction/\" data-wpel", "sources": [{"name": "gmk_center", "url": "https://gmk.center/en/news/norway-plans-to-use-steel-from-decommissioned-ships-for-construction/", "type": "rss"}]}
